# Glass Piano (ADR-0032, ADR-0033): one piano note of the upright pack, taken
# apart in the Spectral Lab and rebuilt when the song loads. Its harmonics are
# a PPG wavetable whose position is where in the note's life you are, from the
# strike to the dark tail, held as long as the key; its hammer is a D-50 attack.
# Scene a picks a moment of the piano per step; scene b lets a slow curve
# wander through it; scene c is the same piano stretched into a bell.
# Needs the sample packs (make samples).
tempo 84
swing 50
setting glass = PpgWave PpgSweepPad: Wt1Table 8, Wt2Table 8, EnvWt -1, Wt1Pos 1, Wt2Pos 0.7
setting hammer = D50 LaFantasia: Pcm1Sample 9
setting bell = PpgWave PpgGlassBell: Wt1Table 9, Wt2Table 9
track glass synth glass
track hammer synth hammer
track bell synth bell
table 1 = upright-piano-kw/C4vH : noise 1.5
table 2 = upright-piano-kw/C4vH : inharmonic 1.6, decay 0.6
attack 1 = upright-piano-kw/C4vH

clip strike = glass .wt1pos("0 ~ 0.6 ~ 0.3 ~ 0.85 ~")
  "c3 ~ g3 ~ d#3 ~ a#2 ~"

clip drift = glass .wt1pos(perlin.slow(4).range(0.2, 0.9))
  "<c3 g3> ~ ~ ~"

clip tick = hammer
  "c3 ~ g3 ~ d#3 ~ a#2 ~"

clip ring = bell .wt1pos(sine.slow(8).range(0, 0.7))
  "<c4 g4 d#4 a#3>"

scene a 4: strike tick
scene b 4: drift tick
scene c 4: ring tick
arrange a b c a
